In the last few pulls from net-next I am seeing an issue where sometimes a =
transfer would stall for about 30secs and then continue. I see this with si=
mple commands like `rsh server uname -a` and ftp transfers. It happens with=
 multiple drivers.

I have not done much digging into it yet, but just wanted to check if it's =
a known issue. I don't see this problem when testing with the torvalds tree=
.

Attached is a capture from the rsh session that fails. The "server" (190.1.=
15.5) is the system running net-next kernel.

Thanks,
Emil


